.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt OSSL_MTC_CA_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_new ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_free ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_add1_cosigner ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_add_revoked_range ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_set_max_serial ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_get0_id ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_cmp ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_find ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_serial
.Nd Merkle Tree Certificate authorities trusted by a relying party
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Lb libcrypto
.In openssl/mtc.h
.Ft OSSL_MTC_CA *
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_new
.Fa "const uint8_t *ca_id"
.Fa "size_t ca_id_len"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *hash"
.Fa "uint64_t min_serial"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *cosigner_pkey"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_free
.Fa "OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_add1_cosigner
.Fa "OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fa "const uint8_t *id"
.Fa "size_t id_len"
.Fa "const char *sig_name"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_add_revoked_range
.Fa "OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fa "uint64_t start"
.Fa "uint64_t end"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_set_max_serial
.Fa "OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fa "uint64_t max_serial"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_get0_id
.Fa "const OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fa "const uint8_t **out_id"
.Fa "size_t *out_id_len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_cmp
.Fa "const OSSL_MTC_CA * const *a"
.Fa "const OSSL_MTC_CA * const *b"
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_MTC_CA *
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_find
.Fa "STACK_OF(OSSL_MTC_CA) *cas"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ca_id"
.Fa "size_t ca_id_len"
.Fa "const char *ca_id_str"
.Fc
.Ft uint64_t
.Fo OSSL_MTC_serial
.Fa "uint16_t log_number"
.Fa "uint64_t index"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An
.Vt OSSL_MTC_CA
object holds what a relying party knows about one
Merkle Tree Certificate authority it trusts:
the CA's trust anchor identifier,
the hash algorithm of its issuance logs,
the public keys whose cosignatures it accepts,
and the serial numbers it considers revoked.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_new
allocates a new object for the CA whose trust anchor identifier is the
.Fa ca_id_len
bytes at
.Fa ca_id ,
in the relative object identifier encoding of the Trust Anchor Identifiers
specification; the bytes are copied.
.Fa hash
is the hash algorithm the CA uses for its Merkle trees.
Serial numbers below
.Fa min_serial
are revoked.
.Fa cosigner_pkey
is the public key that verifies the CA's own cosignature.
The reference count of
.Fa cosigner_pkey
is incremented.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_free
frees
.Fa ca
and drops its references to the keys it holds.
If
.Fa ca
is
.Dv NULL ,
no action occurs.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_add1_cosigner
adds a cosigner whose trust anchor identifier is the
.Fa id_len
bytes at
.Fa id
and whose cosignatures are verified with
.Fa pkey .
The reference count of
.Fa pkey
is incremented.
.Fa sig_name
is ignored.
An identifier equal to the CA's own or to one already added is rejected.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_add_revoked_range
marks the serial numbers from
.Fa start
inclusive to
.Fa end
exclusive as revoked.
The range must be non-empty.
Ranges that overlap or adjoin ranges already added are merged with them.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_set_max_serial
marks all serial numbers above
.Fa max_serial
as revoked.
Until it is called, no serial number is revoked for being too large.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_get0_id
stores a pointer to the CA's trust anchor identifier in
.Pf * Fa out_id
and its length in
.Pf * Fa out_id_len .
The pointer remains valid until
.Fa ca
is freed.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_cmp
orders two CAs by their trust anchor identifiers,
a shorter identifier before a longer one and identifiers of equal length
by their bytes.
It is the comparison function for a sorted
.Vt STACK_OF(OSSL_MTC_CA) .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_find
looks up the CA in
.Fa cas ,
a stack created with
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_cmp
as its comparison function,
whose trust anchor identifier is given either as the
.Fa ca_id_len
bytes at
.Fa ca_id
or, if
.Fa ca_id_str
is not
.Dv NULL ,
as the dotted decimal string
.Fa ca_id_str ,
for example
.Qq 32473.1 .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_serial
returns the serial number of the certificate at
.Fa index
in issuance log
.Fa log_number
of a CA, which is
.Fa log_number
in the top 16 bits and
.Fa index
in the low 48.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_new
returns the new object or
.Dv NULL
on failure, including when
.Fa ca_id_len
is 0.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_add1_cosigner ,
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_add_revoked_range ,
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_set_max_serial ,
and
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_get0_id
return 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_cmp
returns a negative value, 0, or a positive value if the CA at
.Fa a
orders before, equal to, or after the CA at
.Fa b .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_find
returns the matching CA, or
.Dv NULL
if there is none or
.Fa ca_id_str
is not a dotted decimal identifier.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_new 3 ,
.Xr OPENSSL_sk_new 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_load_landmarks 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_parse_certificates 3
